### 1. The Project File (`ExcelToCsvConverter.pro`)

This file tells Qt's build system (`qmake`) what to do. It's automatically generated, but make sure it includes the `widgets` module.

```pro
# Tell qmake which Qt modules to use
QT       += core gui widgets

# Set the target executable name
TARGET = ExcelToCsvConverter

# This is a standard application template
TEMPLATE = app

# Define the source and header files for the project
SOURCES += \
    main.cpp \
    converterwindow.cpp

HEADERS += \
    converterwindow.h
```

---

### 2. The Main Application Entry Point (`main.cpp`)

This file is standard for any Qt application. It creates the application object and our main window.

```cpp
#include "converterwindow.h"
#include <QApplication>

int main(int argc, char *argv[])
{
    // Create the main application object
    QApplication a(argc, argv);

    // Create and show our main window
    ConverterWindow w;
    w.show();

    // Start the application's event loop
    return a.exec();
}
```

---

### 3. The Main Window Header (`converterwindow.h`)

This file defines the user interface class, including the widgets and the functions (slots) that will respond to user actions.

```cpp
#ifndef CONVERTERWINDOW_H
#define CONVERTERWINDOW_H

#include <QMainWindow>
#include <QString>

// Forward-declare the UI classes we'll use as pointers.
// This is a good practice to reduce compilation times.
class QLineEdit;
class QPushButton;
class QTextEdit;

class ConverterWindow : public QMainWindow
{
    // Q_OBJECT macro is mandatory for any class that defines its own signals or slots.
    Q_OBJECT

public:
    // Constructor
    ConverterWindow(QWidget *parent = nullptr);
    // Destructor
    ~ConverterWindow();

private slots:
    // Slot to handle the "Browse..." button click
    void onBrowseClicked();
    // Slot to handle the "Convert" button click
    void onConvertClicked();

private:
    // Helper function to create the UI
    void setupUI();

    // --- The Core Logic ---
    // This function will contain the real conversion logic.
    // We pass it the input Excel file and the directory where CSVs should be saved.
    void processExcelFile(const QString &excelFilePath, const QString &outputDir);

    // Helper function to add messages to our log
    void logMessage(const QString &message);

    // --- UI Member Variables ---
    QLineEdit   *m_pathLineEdit;
    QPushButton *m_convertButton;
    QTextEdit   *m_logOutput;

    // --- Data Member Variables ---
    QString      m_selectedDirectory;
};

#endif // CONVERTERWINDOW_H
```

